-          <t indent="0" pn="section-1.2.2-2">GSS-API callers desiring per-message security services should check
-the relevant service OBJECT IDs at environment establishment time to
-ensure that what is available in the established environment is
-suitable for their security needs.</t>
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-1.2.2-1">Per-IDU security service availability in IDUP-GSS-API is to be understood and used as described in GSS-API <xref target="RFC-2078" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC-2078"/>, with the exception that combinations of services requested by the calling application and supported by the underlying mechanism may be applied simultaneously to any IDU (true for both the SE and the EV calls, but true in the fullest sense for the GP calls).</t>
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-1.2.2-2">GSS-API callers desiring per-message security services should check the relevant service OBJECT IDs at environment establishment time to ensure that what is available in the established environment is suitable for their security needs.</t>
         </section>
