+          <t indent="0" pn="section-2.2.2-10">The PER_CONF return value (in the ret_services paramater) indicates whether the environment supports confidentiality services, and so informs the caller whether or not a request for encryption can be honored.  In similar fashion, the PER_DOA return value indicates whether DOA services are available in the established environment, and the PER_POO and PER_POD return values indicate whether evidence generation services are available.  The TTIME and UTIME values indicate whether trusted time and untrusted time are available for protection / unprotection services.</t>
