-            <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3.2.2-1">The concept of &quot;parameter bundles&quot; is used in the calls presented in
-the following subsections in order to simplify their presentation and
-clarify their intended purpose and use.  See Section 2.3.4.1 for a
-more complete description of parameter bundles.</t>
-            <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3.2.2-2">The following parameter bundles are used in the &quot;SE&quot; protection and
-unprotection sets of calls.</t>
-            <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-2.3.2.2-3">
-              <li pn="section-2.3.2.2-3.1"> Protect_Options PARAMETER BUNDLE
-   o  protect_operation  INTEGER {
-         sign_only              (0),
-         encrypt_only           (1),
-         sign_and_encrypt       (2),
-         -- let mechanism choose order (and readability of signature)
-         sign_then_encrypt_data (3),
-         -- sign, then encrypt plaintext (leaving signature in clear)
